---
interface SpecRow {
  param: string;
  value: string;
}

interface Props {
  rows: SpecRow[];
}

const { rows = [] } = Astro.props;
---
<h2 style="margin-top:32px;">Buyer Specification</h2>
<p>
  The matrix below is confirmed together before quotation — our typical range against your target.
  Where a value reads <em>Confirm specification</em>, we set it to your requirement and document it
  in the quotation.
</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Specification</th><th>Typical / available</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    {rows.map((row) => (
      <tr>
        <td>{row.param}</td>
        <td>{row.value.startsWith("Confirm specification") ? <em>{row.value}</em> : row.value}</td>
      </tr>
    ))}
  </tbody>
</table>
<p class="data-note">
  Values are representative ranges. Packaging (bulk, retail or OEM), MOQ and the document set (COA,
  batch traceability, phytosanitary) are confirmed on inquiry — always confirm your exact target
  specification before a final order.
</p>
